# A known worry about this passage is that "heat" slides between the felt sensation, which is a pain, and a quality in the object, which need not be.
# Here, though, P1 and A1 both speak of the same intense heat, and A1 and C both speak of "the greatest heat perceived by sense".
# So within these statements the claims keep one sense; the worry bears on whether A1 is true, not on the claim changing sense.
